WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.380
- Usually I'll tell you
about something or someone

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:04.360
I'm obsessed with at
this point in the show.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.410
Well, today it's my band who's obsessed.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.500
Their obsession has taken many forms.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.520
Lifeguard, Knight Rider.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.370
That's right.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:16.020
German icon, but he's known
globally as one name, people.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.016
The Hoff, give it up for David Hasselhoff!

00:00:20.016 --> 00:00:25.016
(alternative band music plays)
(audience cheers and claps)

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.066
- It's the Hoff.

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.240
How are you doing?

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.490
- I'm doing fantastic.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.390
What, who's your audience?

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.370
Hello everybody, from.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.730
- Say hello y'all.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.330
I forget how, you're so tall.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.040
Literally every time I'm like, okay.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.690
It's like being around Blake.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.078
So who's the biggest fan in the band?

00:00:50.078 --> 00:00:53.230
- [Band Member] Its Jason.
- Jason is the biggest fan.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.950
I do remember we were on tour in Germany.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:56.783
I believe Berlin.

00:00:56.783 --> 00:00:57.810
And y'all went to the museum.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.643
What was that like?

00:00:58.643 --> 00:00:59.476
- Oh yeah, it was incredible.

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:00.940
I mean, I've been a fan.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.970
I mean, everybody grew
up with Knight Rider

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.550
and I didn't have the
heights but I had some hair,

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.110
and my first car was a black Ford Probe

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.650
'cause I couldn't afford the Trans-Am.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.640
But I mean, I knew he was an actor

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.320
but I had no idea his musical catalog

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.070
until we were all listening
to songs on the bus one night

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.600
and I think it was Lester that pulled out

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.470
one of his rock songs.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.120
I was like, "Oh my gosh, he can sing."

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:20.953
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:20.953 --> 00:01:22.030
- Then we found out about the museum.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.690
Went there, and while we were there,

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:25.230
they had all these signs that he was part

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.550
of the fall of the Berlin wall.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.760
Thought it was a joke,
went home and looked it up.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.610
And it's real.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.460
Like he played a huge part in that.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:32.293
So it just keeps on going.

00:01:32.293 --> 00:01:33.260
So I'm the fan.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.958
- Wait, is that why the
museum is in Berlin?

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:37.560
- The museum is in Berlin

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.500
because I sang to a million
people on new year's Eve.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.333
And I sang,

00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:44.570
♪ I've been looking for freedom. ♪

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.290
And in east Germany, which
wasn't free at that point,

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:49.710
that's all they knew.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.210
And they knew that I was
the guy from Knight Rider

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.780
who sang about freedom.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.510
So I went and sang above a million people

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:57.940
from East and West Germany.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.450
And that's why I became famous in Germany.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:06.047
And then I've been going back
and selling a few records

00:02:06.047 --> 00:02:10.480
and then they ended up
making a museum about me.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:11.810
- I know, but that's got
to be a crazy moment.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.270
You're standing in the center of people

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.000
that literally cannot cross.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.175
The energy of that and all of
them singing the same song,

00:02:18.175 --> 00:02:19.790
that must have been really powerful.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.740
- It was unbelievable because
I went behind the wall

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.190
with a special that
National Geographic did.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:28.700
And I went back and I
met people who escaped

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.250
and I said, "How do you know me?"

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.100
And they went, "I've been
looking for freedom."

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:33.933
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:33.933 --> 00:02:35.440
- And they couldn't sing the next line,

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.922
because they were taught Russian

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:39.439
instead of English in school.

00:02:39.439 --> 00:02:42.100
And it was really tough over there.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.030
- Music is powerful.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:43.970
- It was really tough.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.190
- I do love that music is powerful.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.634
It can unite people.

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:47.930
I believe in that.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:48.763
It sounds cheesy.

00:02:48.763 --> 00:02:50.370
I really do truly believe that.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.160
So wait, do you have something
planned with my band today?

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.790
I heard that you did,
and I'm very excited.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.170
- Yeah, you're missing
something in the show.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.180
And I think that-
- What?

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.157
A theme song, you don't have a theme song.

00:02:59.157 --> 00:03:00.194
- Oh, I don't have a-

00:03:00.194 --> 00:03:04.580
- We have worked up a
few theme songs for you.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.480
- All right.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.180
Can I hear, you want to tell me about one?

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.030
Maybe sing one or?

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:08.930
I don't know.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:10.016
- Let's just sing it.

00:03:10.016 --> 00:03:10.849
Lets sing it.

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:12.432
Okay, let's do it.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.880
You have now given me permission

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:16.790
to use this as my theme.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.630
I'm just saying. (laughs)

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:19.463
'Cause I love it.

00:03:19.463 --> 00:03:20.296
And I'm excited.

00:03:21.283 --> 00:03:22.116
- Hit it, Jason.

00:03:24.643 --> 00:03:29.058
♪ It's time time to watch some Kelly. ♪

00:03:29.058 --> 00:03:31.040
♪ Kelly on the telly ♪

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.368
♪ Its the Kelly Clarkson show ♪

00:03:35.368 --> 00:03:37.282
- You talk about that ending.
(audience cheers)

00:03:37.282 --> 00:03:38.410
All right, all right.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:39.340
I liked it.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.531
I felt the vibe.

00:03:40.531 --> 00:03:41.364
I liked it.
- What do you think?

00:03:41.364 --> 00:03:42.197
What do you think?

00:03:42.197 --> 00:03:43.030
I love it.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.120
I have a feeling I'm
gonna want all of them.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:45.953
- It's for sale.

00:03:45.953 --> 00:03:47.480
I'm gonna literally have,

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.210
I want all of them too like
for different people that call.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.110
Because I feel like you have
a few and I want all of them.

